+/*
+ * A link graph job on a worker core (docs/games/openttd.md, "The link graph on the workers"): upstream runs each in a
+ * thread of its own, on its own copy of the graph, and joins it at a date set when it was spawned; here a job is
+ * handed to a slot, the first core gives the slot to a free worker (or says there is none: the job is then run where
+ * it is first asked about, as before), and the job is finished where upstream joins it. What the job allocates comes
+ * from the slot's heap, never malloc's; what it leaves (its nodes' annotations: the flows) is copied out of that heap
+ * by the core that finishes it, and the heap is used again by the next job.
